decoders:
  stock_fp16           none (today's stream)
  bf16_12              wire only: 5-bit exponent + 7-bit mantissa (sign and low 3 mantissa bits are always 0)
  bf16_10              3-bit exponent offset + 7-bit mantissa; one 5-bit add of a per-matrix exponent base
  dict_lossless        per-matrix dictionary of its distinct fp16 values: 1024 x 16 b RAM per lane, loaded from a matrix header
  cb8                  per-matrix 256 x 16 b LUT (Lloyd, log domain), loaded from a 512 B matrix header
  u8                   uniform log levels: per-matrix 256 x 16 b LUT (or base + k*step into a mantissa ROM)
  ulog8                full-range uniform log: code * step + base (two per-matrix constants) into the mantissa ROM, or a per-matrix 256 x 16 b LUT
  g256                 none: one fp16 scale held for 2 sign beats
  entropy_H0           variable-length entropy decoder at ~2.6 scales/cycle (a bound, not a design)
  entropy_sep_resid    variable-length entropy decoder at ~2.6 scales/cycle (a bound, not a design)
  cb6                  per-matrix 64 x 16 b LUT, 128 B header
  u6                   uniform log levels: per-matrix 64 x 16 b LUT
  ulog6                full-range uniform log: per-matrix 64 x 16 b LUT, 128 B header
  entropy_ctx_left_up  variable-length entropy decoder at ~2.6 scales/cycle (a bound, not a design)
  ulog5                full-range uniform log: per-matrix 32 x 16 b LUT, 64 B header
  bfp4                 as bfp3 with 4-bit codes (a header + 32 codes no longer fit one beat)
  sep4                 sep0 + 4-bit residual: second add of a 16-entry offset table
  sepu4                sep0 + 4-bit full-range uniform residual (16-entry offset table)
  g256_cb8             256 x 16 b LUT, one code held for 2 sign beats
  cb4                  per-matrix 16 x 16 b LUT, 32 B header
  u4                   uniform log levels: per-matrix 16 x 16 b LUT
  ulog4                full-range uniform log: per-matrix 16 x 16 b LUT, 32 B header
  cmp4                 companded full-range levels (density^0.15): per-matrix 16 x 16 b LUT, 32 B header
  g512                 none: one fp16 scale held for 4 sign beats
  bfp3                 block floating point: one scale beat per 32 sign beats = 16-bit header (10-bit top log code, 3-bit shift) + 32 x 3-bit codes; per group one shift, one 10-bit subtract, 64-entry mantissa ROM; no per-matrix tables
  sep3                 sep0 + 3-bit residual: second add of an 8-entry offset table
  sepu3                sep0 + 3-bit full-range uniform residual (8-entry offset table)
  sepc3                sep0 + 3-bit companded full-range residual (8-entry offset table)
  cb3                  per-matrix 8 x 16 b LUT, 16 B header
  ulog3                full-range uniform log: per-matrix 8 x 16 b LUT, 16 B header
  cmp3                 companded full-range levels: per-matrix 8 x 16 b LUT, 16 B header
  bfp2                 as bfp3 with 2-bit codes (80 bits per 32 groups)
  sep2                 sep0 + 2-bit residual: second add of a 4-entry offset table
  sepu2                sep0 + 2-bit full-range uniform residual (4-entry offset table)
  sepc2                sep0 + 2-bit companded full-range residual (4-entry offset table)
  cb2                  per-matrix 4 x 16 b LUT, 8 B header
  g1024                none: one fp16 scale held for 8 sign beats
  sep1                 sep0 + 1-bit residual: second add of a 2-entry offset table
  sep0                 rank-1: 16-bit log code per row + 8-bit log code per group column (G-entry table per matrix); one add, 64-entry mantissa ROM, exponent = high bits
  row_only             one 16-bit log code per row, mantissa ROM
  matrix_const         one scale per matrix (anchor: how much do the scales matter at all)
